       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is twice the maximum labeled sertraline dose.\n\n- **The problem:** The FDA-labeled maximum for adults is 200 mg/day. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function, so there's no renal or hepatic reason to adjust the dose. I don't see a clinical context that would justify 400 mg.\n- **The risks:** At this dose the patient is more likely to have serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, hyponatremia, and activation or agitation. Higher doses haven't been shown to work better.\n\n**Possible options:**\n1. **Sertraline 200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. If the patient is starting treatment, the usual approach is to start at 25\u201350 mg and titrate up.\n2. **A different dose.** Tell me the dose you want.\n3. **400 mg as written.** If you intend this, for example for a specific indication or a patient already on this dose, confirm it. Add a note with the rationale and I'll enter it with that note.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
